# Template for machine-local env values. Copied to .env.local by
# .claude/hooks/session-start.sh in cloud sessions; .env.local is gitignored
# and overrides the committed .env. Public-by-design values (like the Sentry
# DSN) live in .env instead.

# Override the Sentry DSN locally, or set it empty to disable reporting
# entirely on this machine.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# Sentry auth token used ONLY at build time to upload source maps (the
# @sentry/react-native Expo plugin runs `sentry-cli` during release builds;
# without a token the Android/iOS release build fails with "Auth token is
# required"). This is a SECRET — never commit it and never use the
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix (that would ship it in the app bundle). Set it here for
# local release builds (`expo run:android --variant release`). For EAS Build,
# store it as a per-environment secret instead of in this file:
#   eas env:create --name SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN --value <token> --environment production --visibility sensitive
#   eas env:create --name SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN --value <token> --environment preview --visibility sensitive
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=
